**Root cause**

C, `lib/pack/pack.c:170-200` (`fillEdge`): `pt = bz.list[0]; hpt = bz.list[1]; k = 2;` with no size check; the result depends on what follows the one-element allocation. The one-point spline itself comes from `clip_and_install` (`lib/common/splines.c:234`) on overlapping nodes; port and C produce the same spline.

Port, `crates/graphviz-pure-layout/src/pack/mod.rs:499-504`: a one-point spline uses `bz.list[0]` for the missing second point (documented as C undefined behaviour).

Why the port cannot match: the value C reads is out-of-bounds heap memory (it changes with `splines=polyline` vs `splines=spline`, which only changes how the 1-point list was allocated). The port's choice (a degenerate segment at the point) is the defined behaviour C presumably intends. Suggest wontfix; report upstream (fillEdge should check `bz.size`).

A neato reproducer, `repro-neato.gv`, gets its one-point spline from a different source: the self-loop of a zero-size `shape=plain, fixedsize=true` node, which C writes as a single point. Removing that node makes C and the port agree.

```dot
digraph "G" {
layout=neato;
"v35" [shape="plain", fixedsize="true"];
"v22" -> "v22";
"v24" -> "v35";
"v35" -> "v22" [dir="back", fontsize="10.8"];
"v11":"n" -> "v4";
"v7" -> subgraph "s14" {"v24" "v16" "v8"};
"v31" -> "v4";
"v35" -> "v35" [headlabel="end\r中文标签\re=mc²\ry1", penwidth="4.86"];
"v15" -> "v15" [headlabel="…"];
}
```

